 I'm supposed to look at this, interpret these as numbers,

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.920
 and, you know, multiply by 10 and figure out

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.640
 what the hundreds place is, and all that stuff.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.120
 There's a little bit of work to that, and it does it.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.920
 But then it gives us back an integer,

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.160
 and we say, oh, what is that?

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.840
 That's now the 123, but it isn't of type int.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.120
 And now we can add one to it and get 124.

